From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a framed Linux program in front keeps the keyboard

A Linux app opened from its pinned taskbar icon, or from Start, came in
front framed by the shell and took no typing until clicked: its keys went
to the desktop window (linux1's QA VM, 2026-11-27). The session's X window
manager (sg-compositor's) activates the desktop's surface again when a
Linux program's own top-level goes into its frame or the Start menu
closes, and puts the X focus on the desktop window itself.

FocusIn on the virtual desktop's window while the window in front is a
framed Linux program: the X focus goes back into the program, as its
frame has it (WM_X11DRV_SG_EMBED_FOCUS). The person's click on the desktop
makes the desktop the window in front, and the focus stays there.

Gate: test/linuxfocus-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_DESKTOP_TAKES_LINUX_FOCUS).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -930,6 +930,22 @@
     if (event->detail == NotifyPointer) return FALSE;
     if (!hwnd) return FALSE;
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DESKTOP_TAKES_LINUX_FOCUS
+    /* Stained Glass OS 9516: the session's window manager gave the X focus to
+     * the desktop window itself (it activates the desktop's surface again when
+     * a Linux program's own top-level goes into its frame, or the Start menu
+     * closes) while the window in front is a framed Linux program: the focus
+     * goes back into the program, as its frame has it -- its keys went to the
+     * desktop and nowhere (a Linux app opened from its pinned taskbar icon or
+     * from Start took no typing until clicked) */
+    if (is_virtual_desktop() && hwnd == NtUserGetDesktopWindow() && event->mode == NotifyNormal &&
+        foreground && foreground != hwnd && sg_embed_has_child( foreground ))
+    {
+        TRACE( "desktop took the focus from framed %p: given back\n", foreground );
+        NtUserPostMessage( foreground, WM_X11DRV_SG_EMBED_FOCUS, 0, 0 );
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (window_has_pending_wm_state( hwnd, -1 ))
     {
         WARN( "Ignoring window %p/%lx FocusIn serial %lu, detail %s, mode %s, foreground %p during WM_STATE change\n",
